        "subject": "LU-20132 lnet: statically initialize acceptor wait queue",
        "message": "LU-20132 lnet: statically initialize acceptor wait queue\n\nThe LNet acceptor installs lnet_acceptor_ready() as the data_ready\ncallback on each listening socket from lnet_acceptor_add_socket(),\nwhich runs on the LND startup path before the acceptor thread is\nstarted. lnet_acceptor_ready() wakes the acceptor wait queue, but\nthat wait queue was only initialized inside the acceptor thread via\ninit_waitqueue_head(), which runs later.\n\nIf an inbound connection completes its TCP handshake in this window,\nthe listening socket's data_ready callback fires and wakes a wait\nqueue whose list head is still NULL, crashing in __wake_up_common().\n\n  BUG: unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference\n  RIP: __wake_up_common+0x4c/0x190\n   __wake_up_common_lock\n   tcp_child_process\n   tcp_v4_rcv\n\nMove the wait queue to a file-scope variable statically initialized\nat module load with DECLARE_WAIT_QUEUE_HEAD(), so it is always valid\nbefore any listening socket is hooked. Drop the now redundant\ninit_waitqueue_head() in the acceptor thread.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 2e49bc7dd170 (\"LU-18812 lnet: restrict IP addresses that socklnd listens on\")\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I538b66c3954572f13be1963fc887ce136ac922ad\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66829\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Serguei Smirnov <ssmirnov@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Xinxia Qu <xqu@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: Manish Regmi <mregmi@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
